IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `whsact-dates`
IMPORT `whsact-worker`

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (ACT) -- worked cases for the worker's questions in whsact-worker.l4.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names`

`a business` MEANS `a business or undertaking, run alone or with others, for profit or not (including a partnership or an unincorporated association)`
`a volunteer association` MEANS `a volunteer association: volunteers working together for community purposes, none of whom employs anyone to work for it`
`no one` MEANS `no one: I carry out no work for a business or undertaking`
`not police` MEANS `I am not a police officer`
`police on duty` MEANS `I am a police officer, on duty or lawfully performing police functions`
`police off duty` MEANS `I am a police officer, off duty`

`WORKER` MEANS `yes: you carry out work in any capacity for a person conducting a business or undertaking (s 7 (1)), whether as employee, contractor, labour hire worker, outworker, apprentice, student on work experience, volunteer or otherwise`
`WORKER RUNS IT` MEANS `yes: you conduct the business or undertaking yourself and carry out work in it (s 7 (3))`
`POLICE AT WORK` MEANS `yes: a police officer is a worker, and is at work now, being on duty (s 7 (2))`
`POLICE NOT AT WORK` MEANS `you are a worker as a police officer, but not at work while off duty (s 7 (2) (b))`
`NOT WORKER VOLUNTEER ASSN` MEANS `no: a volunteer association does not conduct a business or undertaking (s 5 (6)), so work for it does not make you its worker (the text's no)`
`NOT WORKER` MEANS `no: you carry out no work for a person conducting a business or undertaking (the text's no: s 7 (1)'s "if" fails)`

`no treatment` MEANS `I was not exposed to a substance, or sought no treatment after it`
`a doctor` MEANS `I sought treatment from a doctor`
`a paramedic` MEANS `I sought treatment from a registered paramedic (not a student)`
`someone else` MEANS `I sought treatment only from someone else`

`SERIOUS A` MEANS `a serious injury or illness: it would ordinarily require immediate treatment as an in-patient in a hospital (s 36 (1) (a))`
`SERIOUS B` MEANS `a serious injury or illness: a listed injury for which a person would ordinarily seek immediate treatment (s 36 (1) (b))`
`SERIOUS C` MEANS `a serious injury or illness: a serious head injury or illness (s 36 (1) (c))`
`SERIOUS D` MEANS `a serious injury or illness: treatment sought from a registered health professional within 48 hours after exposure to a substance (s 36 (1) (d))`
`NOT SERIOUS` MEANS `not a serious injury or illness under s 36 (1) (a) to (d); a regulation may prescribe others (s 36 (1) (e)) and is not deposited (NOTHING-kind)`

`N DEATH` MEANS `a notifiable incident: the death of a person (s 35 (a))`
`N SERIOUS` MEANS `a notifiable incident: a serious injury or illness of a person (s 35 (b))`
`N DANGEROUS` MEANS `a notifiable incident: a dangerous incident (s 35 (c), s 37)`
`N SEXUAL ASSAULT` MEANS `a notifiable incident: a sexual assault incident (s 35 (d), s 37A)`
`N NOT ARISING` MEANS `not a notifiable incident: it did not arise out of the conduct of a business or undertaking (the text's no)`
`N NONE` MEANS `not a notifiable incident under s 35 (a) to (d) as far as the Act goes; a regulation may prescribe further serious injuries or dangerous incidents and is not deposited (NOTHING-kind)`
`a shock` MEANS `an electric shock`
`a fall` MEANS `a serious fall (a person falling, or at risk of falling, to a lower level, into a hole, trench, pit, void or water, or onto a dangerous surface or object)`

`IN TIME 48` MEANS `in time: written notice was given within 48 hours of the regulator's requirement (s 38 (4) (b))`
`NOT YET 48` MEANS `not yet given, and the 48 hours have not run out (s 38 (4) (b))`
`LATE 48` MEANS `late: no written notice within 48 hours of the regulator's requirement (s 38 (4) (b))`
`NA 48` MEANS `s 38 (4) (b) does not apply: notice was not given by telephone, or the regulator did not require written notice (the text's no: its "if" fails)`

`MAY STOP` MEANS `yes: you may cease, or refuse to carry out, the work (s 84)`
`MAY NOT STOP` MEANS `no: s 84 does not let you cease work on these facts (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
`PRISONER` MEANS `no: Part 5 does not apply to a worker who is a prisoner in custody in a prison or police gaol (s 103) (the text's no)`
`NOT A WORKER 84` MEANS `s 84 speaks only of workers; it says nothing about you (NOTHING-kind)`

`TELL AND STAY` MEANS `tell the business, as soon as practicable, that you have ceased work under Division 5.6, and remain available to carry out suitable alternative work (s 86 (a), (b))`
`STAY ONLY` MEANS `remain available to carry out suitable alternative work (s 86 (b)); you need not tell the business yourself, because a health and safety representative directed you to stop (s 86 (a))`

`PROTECTED` MEANS `protected: stopping work does not affect the continuity of your engagement for the purposes prescribed by the Regulation (s 88)`
`UNPROTECTED REFUSAL` MEANS `not protected by s 88: you unreasonably failed to do safe and appropriate alternative work you were directed to do (the text's no: its second "if" fails)`
`UNPROTECTED NOT CEASED` MEANS `not protected by s 88: you did not cease work under Division 5.6 (the text's no: its first "if" fails)`

`SUE PART 6` MEANS `yes, for discriminatory or coercive conduct: Part 6 gives a civil proceeding (s 112; see the questions on it)`
`SUE CIVIL PENALTY` MEANS `no: only the regulator or an inspector may bring a proceeding for a WHS civil penalty provision (s 260) (the text's no)`
`SUE PART 7` MEANS `s 267 does not exclude it; whether Part 7 gives you a right is not encoded here (NOTHING-kind)`
`SUE OTHER` MEANS `no: this Act gives you no right to sue for the breach, and does not affect any right you have apart from it, such as a claim in negligence or for workers compensation (s 267) (the text's no)`

§ `s 7 -- Am I a worker`

-- An employee of a company. s 7 (1).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- am I a worker` `a business` FALSE `not police` EQUALS `WORKER`
-- A sole trader who works in her own business. s 7 (3).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- am I a worker` `a business` TRUE `not police` EQUALS `WORKER RUNS IT`
-- A volunteer at a community group with no employees. s 5 (6).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- am I a worker` `a volunteer association` FALSE `not police` EQUALS `NOT WORKER VOLUNTEER ASSN`
-- Someone who does no work for anyone. s 7 (1)'s "if" fails.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- am I a worker` `no one` FALSE `not police` EQUALS `NOT WORKER`
-- Police officers: s 7 (2), on and off duty; the police answer comes first, whoever they work for.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- am I a worker` `no one` FALSE `police on duty` EQUALS `POLICE AT WORK`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- am I a worker` `a business` FALSE `police off duty` EQUALS `POLICE NOT AT WORK`

§ `s 36 -- Serious injury or illness`

-- (a) in-patient.
#ASSERT `s 36 -- was mine a serious injury or illness` TRUE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 EQUALS `SERIOUS A`
-- (b) a listed injury for which a person would ordinarily seek immediate treatment.
#ASSERT `s 36 -- was mine a serious injury or illness` FALSE `a serious burn` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 EQUALS `SERIOUS B`
#ASSERT `s 36 -- was mine a serious injury or illness` FALSE `serious lacerations` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 EQUALS `SERIOUS B`
-- (b) fails when a person would not ordinarily seek immediate treatment.
#ASSERT `s 36 -- was mine a serious injury or illness` FALSE `serious lacerations` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 EQUALS `NOT SERIOUS`
-- (c) a significant blow to the head, whether or not treatment was sought; repeated blows; another serious head injury.
#ASSERT `s 36 -- was mine a serious injury or illness` FALSE `none of these` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 EQUALS `SERIOUS C`
#ASSERT `s 36 -- was mine a serious injury or illness` FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no treatment` 0 EQUALS `SERIOUS C`
#ASSERT `s 36 -- was mine a serious injury or illness` FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `no treatment` 0 EQUALS `SERIOUS C`
-- (d) treatment from a doctor 48 hours after exposure (the last moment within), and from a paramedic after 10 hours.
#ASSERT `s 36 -- was mine a serious injury or illness` FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a doctor` 48 EQUALS `SERIOUS D`
#ASSERT `s 36 -- was mine a serious injury or illness` FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a paramedic` 10 EQUALS `SERIOUS D`
-- (d) fails just after 48 hours, and when treatment is from someone who is not a relevant registered health professional.
#ASSERT `s 36 -- was mine a serious injury or illness` FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a doctor` 49 EQUALS `NOT SERIOUS`
#ASSERT `s 36 -- was mine a serious injury or illness` FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `someone else` 2 EQUALS `NOT SERIOUS`
-- Nothing at all.
#ASSERT `s 36 -- was mine a serious injury or illness` FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 EQUALS `NOT SERIOUS`

§ `s 35 -- Notifiable incident`

-- A death arising out of the business's work.
#ASSERT `s 35 -- is it a notifiable incident` TRUE TRUE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `N DEATH`
-- The same death, not arising out of the conduct of a business or undertaking.
#ASSERT `s 35 -- is it a notifiable incident` FALSE TRUE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `N NOT ARISING`
-- A worker admitted to hospital.
#ASSERT `s 35 -- is it a notifiable incident` TRUE FALSE TRUE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `N SERIOUS`
-- An electric shock that exposed a worker to a serious risk; and the same shock without a serious risk.
#ASSERT `s 35 -- is it a notifiable incident` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 `a shock` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `N DANGEROUS`
#ASSERT `s 35 -- is it a notifiable incident` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 `a shock` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `N NONE`
-- A near-miss fall from a height (a serious fall includes the risk of falling).
#ASSERT `s 35 -- is it a notifiable incident` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 `a fall` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `N DANGEROUS`
-- A suspected sexual assault at the workplace.
#ASSERT `s 35 -- is it a notifiable incident` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 `none of these` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `N SEXUAL ASSAULT`
-- A minor cut: none of the heads.
#ASSERT `s 35 -- is it a notifiable incident` TRUE FALSE FALSE `serious lacerations` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no treatment` 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `N NONE`

§ `s 38 -- Notification`

-- Written notice within 48 hours of the requirement: on the hour, at hour 0, just after.
#ASSERT `s 38 (4) (b) -- was the written notice in time` TRUE TRUE TRUE 48 EQUALS `IN TIME 48`
#ASSERT `s 38 (4) (b) -- was the written notice in time` TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS `IN TIME 48`
#ASSERT `s 38 (4) (b) -- was the written notice in time` TRUE TRUE TRUE 30 EQUALS `IN TIME 48`
#ASSERT `s 38 (4) (b) -- was the written notice in time` TRUE TRUE TRUE 49 EQUALS `LATE 48`
-- Not yet given: 47 hours on, 48 hours on, 49 hours on.
#ASSERT `s 38 (4) (b) -- was the written notice in time` TRUE TRUE FALSE 47 EQUALS `NOT YET 48`
#ASSERT `s 38 (4) (b) -- was the written notice in time` TRUE TRUE FALSE 48 EQUALS `NOT YET 48`
#ASSERT `s 38 (4) (b) -- was the written notice in time` TRUE TRUE FALSE 49 EQUALS `LATE 48`
-- Notice not by telephone, or no requirement.
#ASSERT `s 38 (4) (b) -- was the written notice in time` FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 EQUALS `NA 48`
#ASSERT `s 38 (4) (b) -- was the written notice in time` TRUE FALSE FALSE 100 EQUALS `NA 48`

-- The regulative rule alone: notice at hour 48 fulfils it; at hour 49 it is breached.
#ASSERT `written notice at this hour is in time` 48
#ASSERT (NOT (`written notice at this hour is in time` 49))

-- s 38 (7): 5 years from the day notice is given.
#ASSERT `s 38 (7) -- the last day the record must be kept` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 6 11 2031
-- From 29 February: the last day is 28 February five years on.
#ASSERT `s 38 (7) -- the last day the record must be kept` (`the calendar date` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `the calendar date` 28 2 2029

-- s 38 (9): the identity of a person involved in a sexual assault incident must not be given; other incidents: silent.
#ASSERT `s 38 (9) -- may the business disclose my identity to the regulator` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38 (9) -- may the business disclose my identity to the regulator` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Division 5.6 -- Stopping unsafe work`

-- A scaffolder with a reasonable concern about an immediate fall hazard.
#ASSERT `s 84 -- may I stop unsafe work` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `MAY STOP`
-- The concern would not be found reasonable.
#ASSERT `s 84 -- may I stop unsafe work` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `MAY NOT STOP`
-- A long-term risk, not from an immediate or imminent exposure.
#ASSERT `s 84 -- may I stop unsafe work` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `MAY NOT STOP`
-- No concern at all.
#ASSERT `s 84 -- may I stop unsafe work` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `MAY NOT STOP`
-- A prisoner in custody (s 103), even with a reasonable concern.
#ASSERT `s 84 -- may I stop unsafe work` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `PRISONER`
-- Not a worker.
#ASSERT `s 84 -- may I stop unsafe work` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NOT A WORKER 84`

-- s 85: a direction after consultation that did not resolve the matter; one given at once because it was too urgent;
-- one given without consultation when it was not urgent; one by an untrained representative; one to a worker outside
-- the work group.
#ASSERT `s 85 -- was the direction to stop work one s 85 allows` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85 -- was the direction to stop work one s 85 allows` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 85 -- was the direction to stop work one s 85 allows` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 85 -- was the direction to stop work one s 85 allows` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 85 -- was the direction to stop work one s 85 allows` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))

-- s 86.
#ASSERT `s 86 -- what must I do after stopping work` `on my own concern (s 84)` EQUALS `TELL AND STAY`
#ASSERT `s 86 -- what must I do after stopping work` `on a direction from my health and safety representative (s 85)` EQUALS `STAY ONLY`

-- s 88: no direction; directed and complied; refused unsafe alternative work; refused reasonably; refused unreasonably;
-- did not cease under the division.
#ASSERT `s 88 -- is my continuity of engagement protected` TRUE `the business gave me no direction to do alternative work` EQUALS `PROTECTED`
#ASSERT `s 88 -- is my continuity of engagement protected` TRUE `I was directed to do alternative work and did it` EQUALS `PROTECTED`
#ASSERT `s 88 -- is my continuity of engagement protected` TRUE `I did not do directed alternative work that was not safe or not appropriate for me` EQUALS `PROTECTED`
#ASSERT `s 88 -- is my continuity of engagement protected` TRUE `I did not do safe and appropriate alternative work I was directed to do, and the failure was not unreasonable` EQUALS `PROTECTED`
#ASSERT `s 88 -- is my continuity of engagement protected` TRUE `I unreasonably failed to do safe and appropriate alternative work I was directed to do` EQUALS `UNPROTECTED REFUSAL`
#ASSERT `s 88 -- is my continuity of engagement protected` FALSE `the business gave me no direction to do alternative work` EQUALS `UNPROTECTED NOT CEASED`

§ `s 267, s 272, s 273`

#ASSERT `s 267 -- does the Act give me a right to sue` `Part 6: discriminatory, coercive or misleading conduct` EQUALS `SUE PART 6`
#ASSERT `s 267 -- does the Act give me a right to sue` `a WHS civil penalty provision (Division 13.7)` EQUALS `SUE CIVIL PENALTY`
#ASSERT `s 267 -- does the Act give me a right to sue` `Part 7: workplace entry by WHS entry permit-holders` EQUALS `SUE PART 7`
#ASSERT `s 267 -- does the Act give me a right to sue` `any other provision (for example a health and safety duty in Part 2)` EQUALS `SUE OTHER`

-- A clause "the worker accepts all risk of injury" (excludes); a clause making a labour hire worker responsible for the
-- host's duty (transfers); a clause about something else.
#ASSERT `s 272 -- is the term void` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272 -- is the term void` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272 -- is the term void` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- A charge for safety boots to a worker; a charge to a worker for something else; a charge for safety to a non-worker.
#ASSERT `s 273 -- may the business charge me for safety` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 273 -- may the business charge me for safety` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 273 -- may the business charge me for safety` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
